The Mind Of A Broken Heart 

There I stood, frozen with my eyes focused on the ground.
I thought to myself is this the day? Is this the day I
finally end this cruel life that lived for decades. My 
school looked very small from the ledge of the bell tower.
My school doesn't have those electrial bells, we the bells 
you'd find in a church. It was the tallest building in town,
about 7 stories high. People gathered around the bell tower 
not to look at me but the person at the opposite side of me.
Carl was the popular highschool Football. The one Football 
players who would hook up with one of the smart nerdy
girls and ask to do their homework the next day, some say it's 
true. "Hey aren't you Carl?" I said while turning my head to 
see his face. "And aren't you carmmella, the freak?" he said 
while giggling like a child. "How mature of you" I said 
jokingly while I was thinking about the reasons why he's on 
this ledge in the first place. I was used to being called a 
freak, everyone thinks that about me cause I cause too much 
choas or becasue I use my beauty to get what I want or that 
I'm too smart for my own liking . I broke the silence between 
us, "So why are you here Carl?" I asked curiously. "It's too
much, everything is too much I just want to tear everthing apart 
into peices that can never be recovered or put back together. I've
made too many mistakes and now my heart feels like there's no meaning
in this life or the next, love is so cruel." he said while I moved closer
to him inch by inch. I held his hand knowing what he means, his hands 
are so cold. "You're hands are so cold" I stated. He just blushed and
froze in place. "How about we talk this through?" I asked softly while
laying my head on his shoulder. He noded, so we climbed the ladder down.
As soon as we stepped foot on the ground the crowd applaused for Carl
thinking he saved me from jumping.

A man's mistake is never noticed by himself instantly but only after 
seeing the hurt he has caused. Some peoples' smiles are fake but never
noticed


